<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-basis-dimension" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Basis and Dimension</title>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-basis">
    <title>Basis of a Subspace</title>

    <definition xml:id="def-basis">
      <title>Basis</title>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Let <m>H</m> be a subspace of <m>\R^n</m>. Then
          <m>\{ \vec{u}_1, \ldots, \vec{u}_k \}</m> is called a <term>basis</term> for
          <m>H</m> if the following conditions hold:
        </p>
        <p>
          <ol>
            <li><p><m>\operatorname{Span}\{ \vec{u}_1, \ldots, \vec{u}_k \} = H</m>;</p></li>
            <li><p><m>\{ \vec{u}_1, \ldots, \vec{u}_k \}</m> is linearly independent.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </definition>

    <example xml:id="eg-two-bases">
      <title>Two Different Bases for the Same Subspace</title>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Consider the <m>xy</m>-plane, i.e.,
          <m>H = \left\{ \begin{bmatrix} x \\ y \\ z \end{bmatrix} \in \R^3 \; \middle| \; z = 0 \right\}</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>
          The most obvious basis is
          <m>\mathcal{B}_1 = \{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_2 \}</m>, since
          <m>H = \operatorname{Span}\{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_2 \}</m> and
          <md>
            \vec{x} = x\vec{e}_1 + y\vec{e}_2.
          </md>
        </p>
        <p>
          But it is not the only one. Take
          <m>\mathcal{B}_2 = \{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_1 + \vec{e}_2 \}</m>. Then
          <m>H = \operatorname{Span}\{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_1 + \vec{e}_2 \}</m> and
          <md>
            \vec{x} = (x - y)\vec{e}_1 + y \left( \vec{e}_1 + \vec{e}_2 \right).
          </md>
        </p>
        <p>
          A subspace has many bases <mdash /> but, as we are about to see, they all have
          the same size.
        </p>
      </solution>
    </example>

    <figure xml:id="fig-two-bases">
      <caption>
        Two different bases for the <m>xy</m>-plane <m>H</m>, seen from above:
        <m>\mathcal{B}_1 = \{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_2 \}</m> on the left and
        <m>\mathcal{B}_2 = \{ \vec{e}_1, \vec{e}_1 + \vec{e}_2 \}</m> on the right.
        The pale lines are the grid of each basis: the lines parallel to its two vectors.
      </caption>
      <image width="92%">
        <shortdescription>Two pictures of the xy-plane seen from above. On the left, the basis vectors e 1 and e 2 with a grid of squares; on the right, the basis vectors e 1 and e 1 plus e 2 with a grid of slanted parallelograms.</shortdescription>
        <prefigure label="pf-two-bases" xmlns="https://prefigure.org">
          <diagram dimensions="(557,225)" margins="10">
            <coordinates bbox="(-2.7,-2.2,9.5,2.4)">
              <group at="two-bases">
                <group at="first-basis">
                  <group at="first-basis-grid">
                    <line endpoints="((-2.000,-1.500),(-2.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((-2.500,-1.000),(3.000,-1.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((-1.000,-1.500),(-1.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((-2.500,0.000),(3.000,0.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((0.000,-1.500),(0.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((-2.500,1.000),(3.000,1.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((1.000,-1.500),(1.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((-2.500,2.000),(3.000,2.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((2.000,-1.500),(2.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.000,-1.500),(3.000,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                  </group>
                  <polygon points="((-2.500,-1.500),(3.000,-1.500),(3.000,2.200),(-2.500,2.200))" closed="yes" stroke="#9AA586" thickness="1"/>
                  <group at="first-basis-axes">
                    <line endpoints="((-2.500,0.000),(3.000,0.000))" stroke="#606060" thickness="1" arrows="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((0.000,-1.500),(0.000,2.200))" stroke="#606060" thickness="1" arrows="1"/>
                    <label p="(3.000,0.000)" alignment="nw" offset="(-3,3)"><m>x</m></label>
                    <label p="(0.000,2.200)" alignment="se" offset="(4,-4)"><m>y</m></label>
                  </group>
                  <label at="first-basis-plane" p="(3.000,2.200)" alignment="sw" offset="(-5,-5)"><m>H</m></label>
                  <group at="b1-e1">
                    <line endpoints="((0.000,0.000),(1.000,0.000))" stroke="#4A5D23" thickness="3" arrows="1"/>
                    <label p="(1.000,0.000)" alignment="s" offset="(0,-6)" color="#4A5D23"><m>\vec{e}_1</m></label>
                  </group>
                  <group at="b1-e2">
                    <line endpoints="((0.000,0.000),(0.000,1.000))" stroke="#876801" thickness="3" arrows="1"/>
                    <label p="(0.000,1.000)" alignment="w" offset="(-6,0)" color="#876801"><m>\vec{e}_2</m></label>
                  </group>
                  <label at="first-basis-name" p="(0.250,-1.500)" alignment="s" offset="(0,-6)"><m>\mathcal{B}_1 = \{\vec{e}_1,\ \vec{e}_2\}</m></label>
                </group>
                <group at="second-basis">
                  <group at="second-basis-grid">
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,1.500),(4.500,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,0.500),(5.500,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,-0.500),(6.500,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,-1.000),(9.300,-1.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,-1.500),(7.500,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,0.000),(9.300,0.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((4.800,-1.500),(8.500,2.200))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,1.000),(9.300,1.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((5.800,-1.500),(9.300,2.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
                    <line endpoints="((3.800,2.000),(9.300,2.000))" stroke="#D2D8C2" thickness="1"/>
